13. Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)
user login on website A, then user click a malicious link,  The user's browser automatically includes the authentication token (session cookie) with the malicious request, making it appear legitimate to the web application.

solution
**Anti-CSRF Tokens**: Include a unique token in forms and validate it on the server side. This token should be unique to each session and request.

python django has built-in csrf token, flask use pip install Flask-WTF

Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) is a security feature implemented by web browsers to control how web pages can request resources from a different domain than the one that served the web page. This is essential for protecting users from malicious websites that might try to steal data or perform unauthorized actions on other websites.

from flask import Flask
from flask_cors import CORS

app = Flask(__name__)
CORS(app, resources={
    r"/api/*": {
        "origins": ["http://example.com", "http://anotherdomain.com"],
        "methods": ["GET", "POST"],
        "allow_headers": ["Content-Type", "Authorization"]
    }
})

@app.route('/api/data')
def get_data():
    return {'data': 'This is some data'}

bp = Blueprint('service_api', __name__, url_prefix='/v1')

CORS(bp,
        resources={
            r"/*": {"origins": ["http://example.com", "http://anotherdomain.com"]}},
        supports_credentials=True,
        allow_headers=['Content-Type', 'Authorization', 'X-App-Code'],
        methods=['GET', 'PUT', 'POST', 'DELETE', 'OPTIONS', 'PATCH'],
        expose_headers=['X-Version', 'X-Env']
        )
app.register_blueprint(bp)

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=5001, debug=True)

In this example, CORS is configured to allow requests from `http://example.com` and `http://anotherdomain.com`

CSRF (Cross-Site Request Forgery) and CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) can and often do work together to provide a more secure web application.
CSRF use csrf token to validate requests, CORS Controls which domains are allowed to make requests to your server.


